3. FFmpeg - Separate Runtime Executable
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version: 8.1.2 from pinned Nixpkgs
Upstream Repository: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg

MiniMax H3 media output invokes the headless ffmpeg and ffprobe executables as
separate processes. No FFmpeg library is linked into gufo. The
pinned Nix closure supplies FFmpeg's LGPL/GPL license texts and corresponding
source metadata. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the exact relationship and
enabled-license inventory.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. curl / libcurl - OpenAI-Compatible Evaluation Client
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version: 8.21.0 from pinned Nixpkgs
Upstream Repository: https://github.com/curl/curl

The gufo eval command links libcurl for HTTP and HTTPS model discovery and
chat-completion requests. The pinned Nix closure supplies curl's license text
and corresponding-source metadata. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the exact
relationship.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Evaluation-Only Python Quality Toolchain
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pinned development environments include PyTorch ROCm 2.12.0, Torchvision
0.27.0, and LPIPS 0.1.4 for independent teacher execution and perceptual
quality evaluation. These BSD-licensed packages are not linked into or
distributed with the production Gufo binaries. Their upstream license texts
and source metadata are supplied by the pinned Nix packages; exact
relationships are recorded in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

